{"path":"string/byte/strlen","title":"std::strlen","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>strlen","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/byte/strlen","section":"string","kind":"page","summary":"Returns the length of the given byte string, that is, the number of characters in a character array whose first element is pointed to by str up to and not including the first null character.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/cstring\">&lt;cstring&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> strlen<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> str <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns the length of the given byte string, that is, the number of characters in a character array whose first element is pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">str</span></code> up to and not including the first null character. The behavior is undefined if there is no null character in the character array pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">str</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> str\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to the null-terminated byte string to be examined\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>The length of the null-terminated string <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">str</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Possible_implementation\">Possible implementation</h3>\n<table class=\"eq-fun-cpp-table\">\n<tr>\n<td>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> strlen<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> start<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// NB: start is not checked for nullptr!</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> end <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> start<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">while</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>end <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es5\">\\0</span>'</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>end<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> end <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> start<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstring&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> str<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"dog cat<span class=\"es5\">\\0</span>mouse\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"without null character: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">strlen</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>str<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"with null character: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> sizeof str <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>without null character: 7\nwith null character: 14</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/wide/wcslen\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>wcslen</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the length of a wide string <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/multibyte/mblen\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>mblen</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the number of bytes in the next multibyte character <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/string/byte/strlen\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>strlen</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Possible implementation","id":"Possible_implementation"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"string","title":"Strings library"},{"path":"string/byte","title":"Null-terminated byte strings"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::strlen","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Returns the length of the given byte string, that is, the number of characters in a character array whose first…"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"str"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The length of the null-terminated string str."},{"label":"Possible implementation"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"wcslen","note":"returns the length of a wide string"},{"label":"mblen","note":"returns the number of bytes in the next multibyte character"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":185,"codeBlockCount":3}
